(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_thelivingworld=[{id:"neet-2026r-q114",pn:114,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"The Living World",st:"Taxonomic categories",q:`Match List-I with List-II.
A. Family \u2014 I. Sapindales
B. Genus \u2014 II. Dicotyledonae
C. Class \u2014 III. Anacardiaceae
D. Phylum \u2014 IV. Angiospermae
E. Order \u2014 V. Mangifera
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["A-II, B-I, C-III, D-IV, E-V","A-II, B-III, C-V, D-I, E-IV","A-III, B-V, C-II, D-IV, E-I","A-I, B-V, C-II, D-IV, E-III"],c:2,s:`Mangifera is a genus.
Anacardiaceae is a family.
Sapindales is an order.
Dicotyledonae is a class.
Angiospermae is given as phylum (the publisher notes it should correctly be 'division').
So A-III, B-V, C-II, D-IV, E-I.
Note: Printed 'Answer (3*) (Conceptual errata)': Angiospermae is a division, not a phylum in plants; answer 3 kept.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q127",pn:127,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"The Living World",st:"Taxonomic categories",q:`Arrange the following taxonomic categories in ascending order.
(a) Genus
(b) Class
(c) Order
(d) Phylum
(e) Family
(f) Kingdom
(g) Species
Choose the correct answer from the options given below :`,o:["(a), (c), (d), (g), (f), (b), (e)","(g), (c), (d), (b), (e), (a), (f)","(f), (c), (b), (g), (d), (e), (a)","(g), (a), (e), (c), (b), (d), (f)"],c:3,s:`Ascending order of taxonomic categories:
Species (g), Genus (a), Family (e), Order (c), Class (b), Phylum (d), Kingdom (f).`},{id:"neet-2026-q131",pn:131,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"The Living World",st:"Binomial nomenclature",q:"Which one of the following statements is not true about the universal rules of binomial nomenclature?",o:["Both the words in a biological name, when handwritten, are separately underlined or printed in italics","The specific epithet in the biological name starts with a small letter","The first word in the biological name represents the specific epithet, while the second component denotes the genus","Biological names are generally in Latin"],c:2,s:`By the universal rules, the first word is the genus name and starts with a capital letter.
The second word is the specific epithet and starts with a small letter.
So statement (3), which swaps them, is not true.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q134",pn:134,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"The Living World",st:"Taxonomic categories",q:"Genus represents __________.",o:["a population of plants and animals","a group of closely related species","a group of closely related families","an individual plant or animal"],c:1,s:`A genus is a group of related species.
These species have more characters in common than with species of other genera.`},{id:"neet-2025-q095",pn:95,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"The Living World",st:"Reductionist biology",q:"Which one of the following statements refers to Reductionist Biology?",o:["Physico-chemical approach to study and understand living organisms","Physiological approach to study and understand living organisms","Chemical approach to study and understand living organisms","Behavioural approach to study and understand living organisms"],c:0,s:"The physico-chemical approach to study and understand living organisms is called Reductionist Biology."},{id:"neet-2022-q168",pn:168,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"The Living World",st:"Taxonomic hierarchy",q:"In the taxonomic categories which hierarchical arrangement in ascending order is correct in case of animals?",o:["Kingdom, Class, Phylum, Family, Order, Genus, Species","Kingdom, Order, Class, Phylum, Family, Genus, Species","Kingdom, Order, Phylum, Class, Family, Genus, Species","Kingdom, Phylum, Class, Order, Family, Genus, Species"],a:"4*",s:`No option matches the wording of the question.
The correct ascending order is species \u2192 genus \u2192 family \u2192 order \u2192 class \u2192 phylum \u2192 kingdom.
Option (4) lists these same ranks in the reverse (descending) order.
Note: printed answer 4*; the question says ascending but option 4 is the descending order; no option is truly ascending, so the key follows option 4.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q189",pn:189,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"The Living World",st:"Taxonomic aids: keys",q:`Which of the following are true about the taxonomical aid 'key'?
(a) Keys are based on the similarities and dissimilarities.
(b) Key is analytical in nature.
(c) Keys are based on the contrasting characters in pair called Couplet.
(d) Same key can be used for all taxonomic categories.
(e) Each statement in the key is called Lead.
Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :`,o:["(a), (c), (d) and (e) only","(a), (b) and (c) only","(b), (c) and (d) only","(a), (b), (c) and (e) only"],c:3,s:`A key is a taxonomic aid that is analytical in nature.
It uses contrasting characters in pairs (couplet); each statement is a lead.
(d) is false: different keys are used for different taxonomic categories.`},{id:"neet-2019-q085",pn:85,y:"NEET 2019 \xB7 5 May",tp:"The Living World",st:"Binomial nomenclature",q:"Select the correctly written scientific name of Mango which was first described by Carolus Linnaeus.",o:["Mangifera indica","Mangifera Indica","Mangifera indica Car. Linn.","Mangifera Indica Linn"],c:3,s:`A scientific name has genus and species, and the author\u2019s name is written after it.
Here the author is Linnaeus, written as Linn.
Note: Printed key 4 kept; the species name 'Indica' is printed with a capital I, while the rule is a small letter (Mangifera indica Linn.). The question as printed has this problem.`}]})();
